# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

Set `subject` to manage one subject. Omit it to manage the global level that subjects without their own level inherit.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/resources/axonops_schema_registry_compatibility/resource.tf" }}

## Compatibility levels

| Level | Rule for a new schema version |
|-------|---------------------------------------|
| `NONE` | No checks |
| `BACKWARD` | Can read data written with the previous version |
| `BACKWARD_TRANSITIVE` | Can read data written with all previous versions |
| `FORWARD` | Its data can be read by the previous version |
| `FORWARD_TRANSITIVE` | Its data can be read by all previous versions |
| `FULL` | `BACKWARD` and `FORWARD` with the previous version |
| `FULL_TRANSITIVE` | `BACKWARD` and `FORWARD` with all previous versions |

> **Note:** the AxonOps API cannot reset a compatibility level. `terraform destroy` removes the resource from state but leaves the last level set in the Schema Registry, and shows a warning.

